        "node_id": "n_3_7658c4",
        "thought_text": "The current approach counts numbers with odd digits for all digit lengths up to the number of digits in N, including numbers with an even number of digits. This leads to overcounting. Instead, we should focus only on numbers with an odd number of digits up to N, which can be done by iterating through odd digit lengths and counting numbers within that range.",
